The templates are usefull to build the Linux application
a) hello app created with the help of existing recipes-examples under meta-amd-edf layer
  $ tree ../sources/meta-amd-edf/recipes-examples/
  ../sources/meta-amd-edf/recipes-examples/
  └── hello-world
      ├── files
      │   ├── hello-simple.c
      │   └── Makefile
      └── hello_2.10.bb

b) myapp created by adding custom layer with the recipes-myapp
$ tree ../sources/meta-myapps/
  ../sources/meta-myapps/
  ├── conf
  │   └── layer.conf
  ├── COPYING.MIT
  ├── README
  ├── recipes-apps
  │   └── myapp
  │       ├── files
  │       │   ├── Makefile
  │       │   └── myapp.c
  │       └── myapp_1.0.bb
  └── recipes-example
      └── example
          └── example_0.1.bb

How to create bitbake layers to achive option b)
bitbake-layers --help ==> provide you more details about the options
bitbake-layers create-layer ../sources/meta-myapps
bitbake-layers add-layer ../sources/meta-myapps
bitbake-layers show-layers ==> to cross check that the new layer is added


mkdir -p ../sources/meta-myapps/recipes-apps/myapp/files
vim ../sources/meta-myapps/recipes-apps/myapp/files/myapp.c
vim ../sources/meta-myapps/recipes-apps/myapp/files/Makefile
vim ../sources/meta-myapps/recipes-apps/myapp/myapp_1.0.bb
bitbake myapp

make sure to add the following line in the ./build/conf/local.conf file to pack the applications in to Image

IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " hello"
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " myapp"

